cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use F1-Race, please cite it as below."
title: "F1-Race: minimum-lap-time racing, layer by layer"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "yuanche-auto"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yuanche-auto/F1-Race"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained study of how to drive a racing car around a track as fast as
  possible, built up in layers: optimal racing lines and minimum-time optimal
  control, a dynamic car with tyre slip, model mismatch, random disturbances,
  system identification, reinforcement learning, structural model error, new
  tracks and wet grip, and real-time control, each layer comparing several
  model-based and learning-based methods on the same car, track and test laps.
keywords:
  - minimum-lap-time
  - optimal control
  - model predictive control
  - stochastic MPC
  - system identification
  - reinforcement learning
  - autonomous racing
